## 🟡 Missing Features for "Top-Rated" Status

### 8. No Increment Support in Time Controls

The time control format `"30+0"` suggests `minutes+increment`, but there's no increment logic anywhere. After each move, the active player should receive the increment bonus (e.g., +5 seconds in a `10+5` game).

### 9. No Opening Book / Opening Name Display

Top chess apps show the opening name (e.g., "Sicilian Defense, Najdorf Variation") during the first 10-15 moves. Your engine has no opening book integration.

### 10. No Pre-Move System

In multiplayer, users should be able to queue a move while the opponent is thinking. This is standard in all competitive chess apps and dramatically improves the user experience in bullet games.

### 11. No Move Sound Effects Differentiated by Type

The `AudioPlayer` exists but there's no differentiation between:
- Normal move sound
- Capture sound
- Check sound  
- Castling sound
- Game-over sound
- Promotion sound

### 12. Achievement System is Static

[achievement_model.dart](file:///d:/PP942920DRIVE/PROJECTS/chess/app/lib/data/models/achievement_model.dart) has only 4 hardcoded sample achievements with no unlock logic, no persistence, and no tracking events. The `isUnlocked` field is never updated from gameplay.

### 13. No Eval Bar Widget

`CoachSettings.showEvalBar` exists as a boolean but there's **no `EvalBarWidget`** implementation. An evaluation bar showing the engine's assessment of the position is a signature feature of serious chess apps.

### 14. No Post-Game Analysis Screen

`CoachController.buildPostGameAnalysis()` exists and `GameState.gameCoachHistory` accumulates all move feedback, but there's **no dedicated post-game screen** that lets users replay moves and see per-move classifications. The `GameOverOverlay` only shows aggregate stats.

### 15. No Rematch Logic

The "Rematch 🔄" button in `GameOverOverlay` calls `onPlayAgain` but in multiplayer, this needs to send a rematch request to the opponent via WebSocket. Currently it just navigates locally.

### 16. No Spectator Mode

No mechanism for other users to watch an ongoing game.

### 17. No Anti-Cheat / Move Validation on Server

Moves are sent via WebSocket but never validated server-side. A client could send any arbitrary move.

